==German==
[[File:Forficula_auricularia.jpg|thumb|Ohrwurm (sense 1)]]

===Etymology===
From {{affix|de|Ohr|gloss1=ear|Wurm|gloss2=worm}}. In ancient times, dried and ground animals of the order Dermaptera were used to treat ear diseases, which resulted in the Late Latin name {{m|la|auricula}}. Later the name was in error explained as "worm that enters the ear".

